My requests are being sent with empty params apparently. Let me read one of these response entities to see what was actually sent and figure out the proper format.

Wait — the function is structured as `target OR request`, not both. Let me look at the schema again. Looking at the tool definition:

```
"request": { "description": "inline request content..." }
"target": { "description": "EntityRef-shaped pointer to an existing request entity." }
```

Both are passed as a single object to the tool. Looking at the format, the function takes a single object with `request` (or `target`) as a property of that object. So I should be passing `execute({ "request": { ... } })` not executing with the shape itself.

Looking at the instructions: "pass the request content inline via `request={...}` (one step, preferred)". So I need to call `execute` with argument `request` being the request content.

The function signature is:
```json
{
  "execute": {
    "parameters": {
      "properties": {
        "request": { ... inline request content ... },
        "target": { ... }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

So `execute(request={...})` means calling execute with the parameter "request" set to the inline request content. I was writing it wrong. Let me try again with proper JSON.

